course: dictionary
lesson: 13822
title: Isolation: alone, apart, or kept separate
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Isolation is a noun, and it has three main meanings. It can mean being alone or far away from other people or places. «The lighthouse keeper lived in isolation on a rocky island for ten years.» The keeper had no neighbours nearby, so isolation means being far from others.
explain: Isolation can also mean keeping a sick person or thing apart from others so an illness does not spread. «The sick boy had to stay in isolation at home until the doctor said he was well.» He was kept away from other people to protect them.
explain: In science, isolation means studying one thing alone. «Scientists test one factor in isolation, changing only that one thing.» The phrase "in isolation" means on its own, apart from everything else. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: does it still make sense?
fact: Isolation is a noun, and it is usually uncountable, so we say "a feeling of isolation", not "an isolation".
fact: «Isolation» can mean being alone or far away from other people or places.
fact: In health, «isolation» means keeping a sick person apart from others so an illness does not spread.
fact: In science, «in isolation» means looking at one thing on its own, apart from the other things.
fact: Related phrases include «self-isolation», «feelings of isolation» and «social isolation».
exercise: «The island is far out at sea, and only one boat visits each month.» What does isolation mean in a place like this? | Going to school every day | Being very loud and busy | A type of fishing boat | *Being far away from other places and people
exercise: «The patient had to be kept in isolation so the illness would not spread.» What does isolation mean here? | Going on a long holiday | *Keeping someone apart from others so an illness does not spread | Dancing in a big group | Sharing a room with many friends
exercise: Scientists test one thing in isolation. What does «in isolation» mean? | Mixing everything together and testing it at once | Stopping the test as soon as it starts | Doing the test at the same time as everything else | *Looking at one thing alone, apart from the others
test: Mia felt sad after she moved far from her friends. Which word best describes how she felt? | Hunger | *Isolation | Excitement | Happiness
test: In a science test, what does «in isolation» mean? | *Testing one thing alone, changing only that | Testing nothing at all | Testing outside in the sun | Testing many things at once
exam: Which sentence uses isolation correctly? | Isolation the cake was delicious and sweet | The team had isolation and won the match | *The farm was in isolation, miles from the nearest town | The class had great isolation at the party
